From kasperdanielhansen at gmail.com  Wed Apr  6 15:45:04 2011
From: kasperdanielhansen at gmail.com (Kasper Daniel Hansen)
Date: Wed, 6 Apr 2011 09:45:04 -0400
Subject: [BioC] Script to save plots in Pdf format ( DNAcopy)
In-Reply-To: <27BD4C01-3BF0-4822-A1CA-E1E1CB365F57@dartmouth.edu>
References: <4D9C443C.2080608@hinxton.sanger.ac.uk>
	<27BD4C01-3BF0-4822-A1CA-E1E1CB365F57@dartmouth.edu>
Message-ID: <BANLkTin2d23s8XMFSrLRJgdDOckd7Shidg@mail.gmail.com>

pdf() supports multiple pages so if you do

pdf(file = "tmp.pdf")
plot()
plot()
plot()
dev.off()

you'll get one pdf file with three pages.  Not all devices (example:
png()) support multiple pages.  Essentially, move the loop inside the
pdf() call in the two previous emails.

Kasper

On Wed, Apr 6, 2011 at 9:25 AM, Thomas Hampton
