Hi Gavin,

This probe is classified Bad based on the fact that maps to a
RepeatMasked element of the genome, specifically a LINE repeat in this
case. Previously, we have found repeat mapping probes to be unreliable
(Barbosa-Morais et al NAR 2010) and result in spurious signal. It
would be advisable to take this information into account when
interpreting the data for this probe.

The version of the annotation package you are using annotates any Bad
or No Match probes as NA. However, now is a good time to mention that
the illumina annotation packages that I maintain for Bioconductor 2.8
will have the probe quality and other useful metrics available to the
user.

Regards,

Mark

